// @hash 2c6faa9789cc
{
  // The four arms' contributed field extensions on the merged run list. Each
  // entry is one arm's whole column group, folded in after the nine base
  // columns every kind shares — so this list is the left-to-right order of the
  // table view's arm columns, and the order they appear in the field picker.
  //
  // Every arm field ships `visible: false` (an arm column is blank on all three
  // other kinds' rows, so none of them earns a default column). The order
  // therefore governs the reading order of the picker, and of the columns once
  // someone turns them on.
  //
  // NOT alphabetical, which is what the seed produced — that ordered by plugin
  // id (`apps.deploy…` first), which is an artefact of where the code lives and
  // says nothing about how the surface reads. Ordered instead by how close each
  // arm sits to the reader:
  //
  //   build    — first, because this surface's primary hosts ARE the build
  //              popover and /debug/build. A build row's own columns should sit
  //              nearest the shared ones a reader has just scanned.
  //   release  — then the shipping pair, in pipeline order.
  //   deploy   — after release on purpose: `deploy.releaseRunId` points INTO
  //              the release arm, so a reader following that link scans forward
  //              rather than doubling back.
  //   backup   — last. Host-global and orthogonal to build → release → deploy,
  //              and it has its own pinned surface (the Backup panel) where its
  //              columns are the thing you came for, so it earns its place here
  //              least.
  //
  // Node forms, for whoever edits this next:
  // Item: "<key>" (terse; <key> is "<pluginId>:<id>")
  // Hide: { "item": "<key>", "hidden": true }
  // Spacer (gap): { "type": "spacer", "id": "<unique-id>" }
  // Group: { "type": "header", "label": "<title>", "collapsed": false, "items": [ "<key>", … ] }
  // Overflow (⋯ menu): { "type": "overflow", "id": "<unique-id>", "items": [ "<key>", … ] }
  "items": [
    "build.runs-arm:build",
    "release.runs-arm:release",
    "apps.deploy.deployments.runs-arm:deploy",
    "backup.runs-arm:backup"
  ]
}
